Title: Change nightbeat-supervisor timer to hourly at H+30
Created: 2026-05-13
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-13T20:40Z claude created
2026-05-13T20:46Z claude note updated timer: every-15-min → hourly at :30

--- body ---
## Context

`claude-nightbeat-supervisor.timer` currently fires every 15 minutes:

```
OnCalendar=Mon..Fri *-*-* 22,23,0,1,2,3,4,5,6:0,15,30,45:00
OnCalendar=Sat,Sun *-*-* *:0,15,30,45:00
```

The beat timer (`claude-nightbeat.timer`) fires hourly at `:00` (±5 min
`RandomizedDelaySec=300`). The supervisor's job — merge ready PRs, diagnose
failures — does not benefit from 4× frequency: beat only produces new outcomes
once per hour. Three of every four supervisor cycles see no new data and write
`action=idle` to the journal.

Firing at `:30` instead puts the supervisor at the midpoint of the beat cycle.
Beat completes well before :30, so the supervisor always surveys a full hour of
outcomes rather than a partial one.

## Actions

1. In `systemd/claude-nightbeat-supervisor.timer`, replace the `:0,15,30,45`
   cadence with `:30`:
   ```
   OnCalendar=Mon..Fri *-*-* 22,23,0,1,2,3,4,5,6:30:00
   OnCalendar=Sat,Sun *-*-* *:30:00
   ```
   Keep `RandomizedDelaySec=30` (avoids exact collision with anything else at
   :30) and `Persistent=true`.
2. Update the `[Unit] Description` to reflect the new cadence:
   "Nightbeat supervisor — hourly at H+30 during nightbeat window"
3. Install the updated unit on all machines that run nightbeat:
   ```bash
   cp systemd/claude-nightbeat-supervisor.timer \
      ~/.config/systemd/user/claude-nightbeat-supervisor.timer
   systemctl --user daemon-reload
   systemctl --user restart claude-nightbeat-supervisor.timer
   ```
4. Verify with `systemctl --user list-timers claude-nightbeat-supervisor.timer`
   that NEXT shows a :30 trigger.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `systemd/claude-nightbeat-supervisor.timer` fires at `:30` only
- [ ] `systemctl --user list-timers` shows next trigger at H+30
- [ ] Unit description matches new cadence
- [ ] Installed on padme (and doudou if applicable)
